cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Frost: Incremental GNN Inference for Geometric Rollouts"
abstract: >-
  Edge-local caching with conservative-by-construction staleness for
  machine-learned interatomic potentials and learned physics simulators.
  Frost treats the message-passing state of a rollout GNN as a cache whose
  invalidation predicate is derived from the physics of atomic motion, so that
  energy drift admits a proved bound rather than an empirical hope.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0-dev
date-released: "2026-09-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shashank/frost"
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - machine-learned interatomic potentials
  - equivariant graph neural networks
  - incremental computation
  - inference systems
authors:
  - name: "The Frost Authors"
